   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\"><span class=\"kind\">function</span> Flush <span class=\"sws\"><a href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_LogAndTrace.pdf#nameddest=SWS_LOG_00039\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_LogAndTrace.pdf)\">[SWS_LOG_00039]</a></span> <span class=\"ups\">Upstream: <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/FO/AUTOSAR_FO_RS_LogAndTrace.pdf#nameddest=RS_LT_00003\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_FO_RS_LogAndTrace.pdf)\">RS_LT_00003</a>, <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/FO/AUTOSAR_FO_RS_LogAndTrace.pdf#nameddest=RS_LT_00049\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_FO_RS_LogAndTrace.pdf)\">RS_LT_00049</a></span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">void Flush () noexcept;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Sends out the current log buffer and initiates a new message stream. Note: Calling <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_log_LogStream_2f1f1b.html#SWS_LOG_00039\">ara::log::LogStream::Flush</a> is only necessary if the <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_log_LogStream_2f1f1b.html\">ara::log::LogStream</a> object is going to be re-used within the same scope. Otherwise, if the object goes out of scope (e.g. end of function block) then the flushing operation will be done internally by the destructor. It is important to note that the <a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_log_LogStream_2f1f1b.html#SWS_LOG_00039\">ara::log::LogStream::Flush</a> command does not empty the buffer, but it forwards the buffer’s current contents to the Logging framework.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
